# spring — candidate palette, same derivation as cool.env:
# matplotlib's `spring` colormap sampled at t = 0, .25, .5, .75, 1 and
# pastelised toward white at strength 0.68; the alert pair at 0.25. The dark
# neutrals carry the ramp's own hue so the palette reads as one family.
COOL_BG0=#281B1B
COOL_BG1=#3D2D2D
COOL_BG2=#533E3E
COOL_FG0=#FFF6F6
COOL_FG1=#FFD6D6
COOL_DIM=#FFC6C5
COOL_DIMMER=#FFB9B9
COOL_0=#FFADFF
COOL_1=#FFC2EB
COOL_2=#FFD6D6
COOL_3=#FFEBC2
COOL_4=#FFFFAD
COOL_HOT_0=#FF40FF
COOL_HOT_4=#FFFF40
COOL_MINT=#FFC2EB
COOL_BLUSH=#FFEBC2
COOL_ACCENT=#FFADFF
COOL_ACTIVE=#FF40FF
COOL_URGENT=#FFFF40
COOL_WARN=#FFEBC2
COOL_GOOD=#FFC2EB
COOL_INACTIVE=#533E3E
